              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Using strings as booleans in Python has unexpected results.\n`\"one\" and \"two\"` will return \"two\".\n`\"one\" or \"two\"` will return \"one\".\n In Python, strings are truthy, and strings with a non-zero length evaluate to True.\n"
              },
